@[spell-caches step]
Select the spell caches (built packages) on the ISO that you want installed on
top of the basesystem; they are in /var/cache/sorcery/.

Boot loader: @[grub2] (BIOS and UEFI) is the only one on the ISO. Select it if
you want GRUB; otherwise leave it out and set up another one in the boot-loader
step (systemd-boot comes with @[enchantment install init systemd]; Limine,
rEFInd, SYSLINUX and LILO are cast there with network; see @[todo boot-loader]).
On UEFI machines also select @[efibootmgr] and @[dosfstools] (fsck.vfat for the
EFI system partition), whichever boot loader you choose.

Then add the tools for your filesystems (@[xfsprogs], @[btrfs-progs]) and
anything else you like (e.g. @[openssh], or @[vim] and @[jed] next to the base
system's nano). The menu lists these main caches;
the others in /var/cache/sorcery are only their dependencies, which are added
automatically when they are installed (@[add] still takes any of them by name).

  @[enchantment select caches]              # menu: space toggles, enter accepts
  @[enchantment select caches show]         # list the selection
  @[enchantment select caches add 'grub2*'] # add files matching a pattern
  @[enchantment select caches del 'grub2*'] # remove files matching a pattern
  @[enchantment select caches all]         # (or none) all or nothing

The selection is a plain list of file names, one per line, which you can also
edit directly: @[$EDITOR $ENCHANT_TMP/spell-caches]

You can change it at any time until you install the caches in the basesystem
step. When you are finished selecting, type @[next].
